1
00:00:03,205 --> 00:00:08,039
Most serious injuries at work follow near misses that someone saw and never

2
00:00:08,039 --> 00:00:12,745
reported, because reporting was slow or felt like telling on a colleague.

3
00:00:13,195 --> 00:00:17,089
Near-Miss is a Fabric App where every hazard on a site is a

4
00:00:17,089 --> 00:00:20,785
pin on its plan, coloured by how bad it could have been.

5
00:00:21,851 --> 00:00:26,101
The status lens shows what is new, triaged, or waiting

6
00:00:26,101 --> 00:00:29,801
on a fix; fixed hazards shrink to a check mark.

7
00:00:30,251 --> 00:00:34,539
The heat lens weights every report by its potential, and the

8
00:00:34,539 --> 00:00:38,541
loading dock is the top hotspot of the last ninety days.

9
00:00:39,352 --> 00:00:42,944
Replay the ninety days and watch it form: forklifts and

10
00:00:42,944 --> 00:00:46,862
people crossing at the same dock doors, report after report.

11
00:00:47,312 --> 00:00:49,690
Then the barrier and the signal crossing

12
00:00:49,690 --> 00:00:51,712
went in, and the heat cooled away.

13
00:00:52,519 --> 00:00:56,932
Today ranks what needs attention now: a serious near miss is

14
00:00:56,932 --> 00:01:01,419
past its four-hour triage limit, and seven fixes are overdue.

15
00:01:02,224 --> 00:01:05,137
View it as a supervisor for your own site, or as a

16
00:01:05,137 --> 00:01:08,574
reporter to see your own reports and what happened to them.

17
00:01:11,826 --> 00:01:14,660
Reporting takes a few taps: where on the

18
00:01:14,660 --> 00:01:17,706
plan, what kind, how bad, and one sentence.

19
00:01:18,156 --> 00:01:22,356
Report anonymously and the name is not stored at all, so

20
00:01:22,356 --> 00:01:26,406
nobody, not even the safety lead, can see who sent it.

21
00:01:26,856 --> 00:01:29,661
The honest trade-off is that nobody can edit

22
00:01:29,661 --> 00:01:31,956
it afterwards, and the form says so.

23
00:01:32,765 --> 00:01:36,592
The site supervisor triages it, but a serious report cannot

24
00:01:36,592 --> 00:01:39,705
be fixed or closed until someone owns an action.

25
00:01:40,155 --> 00:01:42,984
Assign the fix to an owner; the due

26
00:01:42,984 --> 00:01:46,945
date defaults by potential, two days for serious.

27
00:01:48,154 --> 00:01:52,434
For the start of a shift, the toolbox talk prints one page on

28
00:01:52,434 --> 00:01:57,064
a zone: what was reported, what was fixed, and what to talk about.

29
00:01:57,865 --> 00:02:01,476
Report it in thirty seconds, fix it before anyone gets hurt,

30
00:02:01,476 --> 00:02:04,725
and let the plan show you where the risk is gathering.
